{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישכון", :translit "v'yishkon", :gloss "and He/it dwelt"} {:he "וישכון הענן במדבר פארן", :translit "v'yishkon he'anan b'midbar pa'aran", :gloss "and the cloud dwelt in the wilderness of Paran"} {:he "וישכון ישראל בטח בדד", :translit "v'yishkon yisrael betach badad", :gloss "and Israel dwelt securely alone"} {:he "וישכון בירושלם", :translit "v'yishkon b'yerushalayim", :gloss "and He/it dwelt in Jerusalem"} {:he "וישכון ערים נכחדות", :translit "v'yishkon arim nichadot", :gloss "and He/it dwelt desolate cities"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["וישכון" "וישכון הענן במדבר פארן" "וישכון ישראל בטח בדד" "וישכון בירושלם" "וישכון ערים נכחדות"]}], :frame {:text "The five occurrences of וישכון trace a trajectory: the glory that dwelt at Sinai accompanied Israel afterward, dwelt securely when Israel was faithful (Numbers 24:21–22 parallels Israel dwelling alone), and was destined to dwell in Jerusalem. But when Israel sinned, the dwelling turned to desolation (Isaiah 13:20–21, where ערים נכחדות appears) and the Shekhinah withdrew from the Temple. Ezekiel 10–11 describes the departure of the glory of YHWH from the Temple before its destruction, and Ezekiel 43:1–5 promises its return.", :sources ["Isaiah 13:20" "Ezekiel 10:18" "Ezekiel 11:23" "Ezekiel 43:2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 5, :occurrences ["וישכון" "וישכון הענן במדבר פארן" "וישכון ישראל בטח בדד" "וישכון בירושלם" "וישכון ערים נכחדות"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וישכון", :refs ["Job 15:28"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וישכון הענן במדבר פארן", :refs ["Numbers 10:12"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "וישכון ישראל בטח בדד", :refs ["Deuteronomy 33:28"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "וישכון בירושלם", :refs ["1 Chronicles 23:25"], :n 1, :lens :plene-insensitive} {:phrase "וישכון ערים נכחדות", :refs ["Job 15:28"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :discip